{"c":[{"id":"af620a5eca93aec7","sum":"H6-R3: guest file URLs must name real files; stop the router before Helper.shutdown; ghost runs type into a fresh TextEdit; rig cua-driver alerts cover windows; replayed typing needs value+focusedKey in one snapshot; corpus incoming-line moments use the fake clock.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"968935f1f64b4697","sum":"H6-H7b: guest file URLs: seed real files as Finder does; stop the router before Helper.shutdown in scripts; on-screen ghost runs type into a fresh TextEdit; in the rig, cua-driver get_window_state raises a covering alert, so read AX with a17-tool value.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"f9874c6fb70cb129","sum":"H7b: in the VM a public.file-url naming a missing file is seen only by its writer; seed file URLs as Finder does. H6: Helper.shutdown leaves the router live: in-process scripts stop it first (routing_option.ts stop), or a late observe hits closed stores.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T133211Z-f47f4f8a4eaf4829","text":"H7b: on the VM guest's general pasteboard a public.file-url naming a missing file is seen only by its writer; other processes (Caret, a17-tool dump) never list it, count unchanged (A17 race00, plain05-09). Seed file URLs as Finder does: NSURL of a real file.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T143020Z-7e9c54758649b0bf","text":"H6: Helper.shutdown leaves the router live: in-process scripts stop it first (routing_option.ts stop: shadow, cancel timers, await idle), or a late observe hits closed stores and ends the run ('statement has been finalized').","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"2bbdec88d0b9e745","sum":"H6/H7b: on-screen ghost runs type into a fresh TextEdit (caret-fixture's field gave few value reads). In the rig guest cua-driver get_window_state raises a bypass alert that covers windows (offers held covered); read AX with a17-tool value.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T143020Z-8eb592e9f22ab7a6","text":"H6: on-screen ghost runs type into a fresh TextEdit instance; caret-fixture's single-line field gave the host almost no value reads. With pid-posted keys both reader and host saw TextEdit's field come and go 20+ times in 130 keys.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T152850Z-7c0a9e0204dd886b","text":"H7b: in the rig guest, cua-driver get_window_state raises macOS's 'CuaDriver ... bypass the system private window picker' alert (UserNotificationCenter, layer 8); it stays up and covers windows, so Caret holds offers as covered. Read AX values with a17-tool value.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"ac3096d5776075d7","sum":"R2-R3 routing: replayed typing needs its value in the same snapshot; no focusedKey makes Router 1 abstain; Router 1 skipped only for consentedCandidates offers (routing/consent.ts); run incoming-line corpus moments on the fake clock.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"8c07db9d1f57e7f4","sum":"R2: replayed typing must carry its typed value in the same snapshot as the text, or no breakpoint opens and no event card lists; a recorded snapshot without focusedKey makes Router 1 abstain (A5's offers-loop.ndjson lacked it until 831ab47).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T155131Z-2d735fed11dec073","text":"R2: scripts that replay typing must send a typed value (snapshot values) in the same snapshot as its text: a value that arrives after the sentence boundary opens no breakpoint, so the event card is never listed.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T155131Z-b3055d198779a6ea","text":"R2: a recorded snapshot without the reader's focusedKey makes Router 1 read 'the cursor is not in a text field' and abstain; A5's offers-loop.ndjson lacked it until 831ab47, which is why H6 saw the loop abstain.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"3b5d87e819a193ac","sum":"R2-R3: Router 1 is skipped only for offers consentedCandidates builds on a held offer's record (routing/consent.ts; those messages count only from a host session); corpus-eval --real-clock never waits the router cooldown, so run incoming-line moments on the fake clock.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T155145Z-05c6fed3ed39acff","text":"R2: Router 1 is skipped only for offers Helper.consentedCandidates builds on a held offer's own record (routing/consent.ts). Messages that write such records (skillAnswer, resume, skills/ save, watch role) count only from a host session.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T170330Z-3e0249266797e51f","text":"R3: corpus-eval --real-clock settle() does not wait the router cooldown timer, so an incoming line's later context is never scored; run incoming-line moments on the fake clock.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"592a384cd6680d71","sum":"R3-G2: jev.holding tests await a flush; Jev judges state on short criteria; Router 1's task question is separate; no routingContext for a plain caret; goals done only with left[] empty; pick goal values by quoted part; goal writes pass goals/gates.ts.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"71181bfecc426109","sum":"R3: await a flush not coord.idle() under jev.holding; Jev judges state against short criteria (rule in instructions); Router 1's task question is a separate request; corpus m36/m43/m37 misses are event-card code, not the router.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"5a582d7c7a76d2a6","sum":"R3: with jev.holding, await a flush not coord.idle() (a stale reply frees the slot); Jev judges the request state against short criteria: what it judges goes in state, the rule in instructions (task question with the sentence in the act option split ~50/50).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T170330Z-4f977dd1bf6c45f7","text":"R3: coordinator tests with jev.holding: a stale reply now frees the slot and the next field's call starts at once, so await a flush, not coord.idle(), while a call is held (idle would wait on the held call).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T170330Z-539f47d0a41290db","text":"R3: Jev (System One) judges the request state against short criteria; put what it judges in state and the rule in instructions. Router 1's task question with the sentence inside the act option split ~50/50 (r3 task-wording probe 8/14 vs 14/14).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"a2301c765553cede","sum":"R3: Router 1's task question is its own request after the outcome question (one shared state moved m34 write 0.75 to 0.32); corpus m36/m43/m37 misses are event-card code (no date anchor, no person), not the router.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T170330Z-75585e5911775e88","text":"R3: Router 1's task question (judge.ts) is its own request after the outcome question; with the offer in one shared state the outcome answers moved (corpus m34 write 0.75 -> 0.32).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T170330Z-9c33f255f5c1caad","text":"R3: corpus m36/m43 list no event card by the producer's rule (a conversation line's relative date has no anchor); m37 finds no person. Those misses are event-card code, not the router.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"21f781157288bdd8","sum":"R3-G2: no routingContext for a plain caret ('unknown' reads as caret); goals are done only with left[] empty; pick goal values by their quoted part; every goal write passes goals/gates.ts, and desk tests use test/goal-desk.ts standInJev.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"711ded7100cb3d56","sum":"R3-G2: RouteFollower sends no routingContext for a plain caret, so context.ts reads 'unknown' as caret; GoalProgress is done only when left[] is empty, and runs.ts owes every required or recipient field left.ts marks in windows a goal writes in.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T170330Z-dcc2d733c48b884a","text":"R3: RouteFollower sends no routingContext while the selection is a plain caret, so routing/context.ts treats the helper's 'unknown' selection as caret; comparing them ended every write session at the host's first sentence end.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T173412Z-100b242cff553f5d","text":"G2: GoalProgress finished is done only when left[] is empty (partial/handoff otherwise); runs.ts owes every field left.ts marks required or recipient in windows a goal writes in, and a closed window leaves them unresolved.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"9acdbaecfe2a51ce","sum":"G2: a goal value's display names its source window's title, so goal-prompt.ts says pick values by their quoted part; every goal write passes goals/gates.ts, lowerGoal needs askJev + ledger, and desk tests pass test/goal-desk.ts standInJev.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T173412Z-33695164e4940cad","text":"G2: a goal value's display names its source window's title, so live qwen3.8 matched v.display.includes('ORD-...') to the sender's email; goal-prompt.ts now says pick values by their quoted part.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T173412Z-c65516aec96de620","text":"G2: every goal write passes goals/gates.ts (never-typed, misfit + numberFieldMisfit, Ask's verifyWrites Jev question); lowerGoal is async and needs askJev + ledger; with no Jev a goal writes no copied value, so desk tests pass test/goal-desk.ts standInJev.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
